Learning Styles
• How would you describe your preferred learning style?
• Can you give examples of how you use this style in your studies?
Follow-up:
• What specific activities or resources do you find most helpful for your learning style?
Student 1: “So maybe my preferred learning style is a combination of visual and reading or
writing. So when I say visual, so I am a visual learner. So I learn more effectively if there is visual,
there is a visual in the book or there is a powerpoint presentation being used. And also reading
and or writing because while the discussion, while the discuss because I am taking down notes.
Yeah, so I take down notes during our discussion and sometimes I rewrite them in a more
organized way using highlighters, highlighting those terminology that are important that I feel
are possible to use in the exam. And sometimes, I also like watching educational YouTube videos
to visualize the topics we discuss like to understand. “
Student 2: (Cebuano) "Both visual and auditory, but more sa visual. Sa visual learning style
kay,or medyo kay, not sure if similar ba ni sa obang taw kay Whenever mag-discussion, need
gyud ata like present ang teacher para sa akoa. So gusto ko naay fucos sa discussion,even
listening usahay dli ko ka focus. Need kog visual presentation para makasabot ko sa lesson. Ang
graphic organizers, nakatabg gyud sa akoa. Akong mga notes is form of graphic organizer."
(English ) "Both visual and auditory, but more on visual. In my visual learning style,
or a little bit, I'm not sure if it's similar to others. Whenever there's a discussion, the teacher really
needs to be present for me. I want to focus on the discussion, even listening sometimes I can't
focus. So, I need a visual presentation so that I can understand the lesson. The graphic organizers
it really suits me. My notes are form of graphic organizer."
Student 3: (Cebuano) “Ako gyud nga learning style kay visual learner ko. Mas dali ko kasabot
kung naay pictures, diagrams, charts or videos. Ganahan pud ko magbasa-basa ug mga notes
nga naay highlights para klaro akong guide. Kung mag study ko, akong buhaton kay magtan-aw
ko sa ppt sakong teacher, then magbuhat ko ug summary notes gamit highlighters. Mag drawing
pud ko ug concept maps. Helpful gyud kaayo ang mga powerpoint presentations sa teachers.
Ganahan pud ko kung naay group activities nga naay visual outputs like posters mga inana.”
(English) “My learning style is a visual learner. I understand more easily if there are
pictures, diagrams, charts or videos. I Also, I like to read notes that have highlights so that I can
have a clear guide. When I study, I do it by looking at my teacher's ppt, then I make summary
notes using highlighters. I also draw concept maps. Powerpoint presentations are really helpful
for teachers. I also like when there are group activities that have visual outputs like posters like
that.”
Student 4: “I am a visual-auditory learner. I can retain information when I can see visuals and
explicit instruction at the same time. And this help me in studying because I can understand the
lesson well. For example, in an activity using powerpoint presentation.
Student 5: “I described my learning style as both visual and auditory, because if, in terms of
