 Adaptation and Improvement
• How do you adapt your learning style when it is not supported in the classroom?
• Can you describe any strategies you use?
Follow-up:
• Have these strategies been effective? Why or why not? What changes would you suggest
to improve the classroom environment for better learning style adaptation?
• How do you think these changes would impact your learning experience?
Student 1: “I watch YouTube videos that are related to our topic so that I can review our topic. I
do summarize my topic.
Student 2: (Cebuano) "Usually naa man nay e hatag self-study notes ang mga teacher. Ako nlang
na sya e summarize para mas makasabot ko. Ang pinakadako gyud nakatabang sa akoa kay
further reading gani after discussion. Usahay basahon naku ang ge send ang ppt's. Yes, effective
sya para naku."
(English) “Teachers usually give self-study notes, I'll just summarize it so I can
understand it better. The thing that helped me the most was further reading after discussion.
Sometimes I read the ppt's sent by instructors. And yeah, it's effective for me."
Student 3: (Cebuano) “Kung usahay dili ma-support akong learning style, ako buhaton kay
magbasa-basa ko daan sa lesson before mo-sulod sa klase, then mag research ko sa YouTube or
Google. Mag note-taking pud ko sa mga important points kay mao gyud na makatabang nako nga
mas makasabot ko. Aside sa note-taking, ako pud i-try ug explain sa akong self ang topic, like
mag pretend ko nga teacher ko then i-discuss nako sa imaginary students. Sometimes mag ask
pud ko help sa akong mga classmates nga kasabot na daan. Yes effective siya para nako kay mas
ma retain nako ang information kung ako mismo ang mo-explain. Dili lang ko ga rely sa lecture,
kay sometimes limited ra ang time sa discussion. Unta madungagan pa ang electric fans or ma
consider nga aircon kay grabe jod ang kainit usahay. Pwede pud unta ma install ug blinds or
curtains para dili kaayo sakit sa mata ang light. And unta naay access sa digital tools like
projector para sa mga visual learners. Makatabang gyud siya ug dako kay kung comfortable ang
room, mas ma-focus ko. Dili nako mag sige'g hunahuna nga init or samok. Mas productive gyud
ang learning experience.”
(English) "If sometimes my learning style is not supported, I do it by reading the
lesson before entering the class, then I do research on YouTube or Google. I also take notes on
important points because that really helps me understand better. Aside from note-taking, I also
try to explain the topic to myself, like I pretend to be my teacher and then I discuss it with
imaginary students. Sometimes I also ask for help from my classmates who already understand.
Yes, I can retain the information myself, because the time is limited in the discussion. I hope
electric fans will be added or an aircon. I wish I could install blinds or curtains so that the light
is not too painful for the visual learners. I can focus more. I can't go on think heat or trouble. The
learning experience is really more productive.”
